-- ============================================================================
-- The Neverhood - per-scene palette association
--
-- Most bitmaps in the BLB archives carry no embedded palette: of 1379 bitmaps
-- only 298 have one. The remaining 1081 surfaces (sprites, mice, fonts, cursors,
-- UI pieces) are drawn over a scene background and borrow that background's
-- palette. Scene composition is not stored in the data - it lives only in the
-- compiled game code - so this table was derived offline by cross-referencing
-- the ScummVM Neverhood module sources (engines/neverhood/modules/*.cpp,*.h):
--
--   * each scene constructor sets its palette via setBackground(hash)/
--     setPalette(hash) (the background bitmap holds the scene palette);
--   * the entities it inserts borrow it: insertStaticSprite(0x...),
--     insertSprite<Class>(0x...), insertScreenMouse/insertPuzzleMouse/
--     insertNavigationMouse(0x...), createStaticScene(bg, cursor),
--     loadSprite(0x...), class names embedding a scene number (SceneNNNN,
--     AsSceneNNNN...), and file-scope hash arrays named after the scene
--     (kSceneNNNN*, kSsSceneNNNN*).
--
-- The result maps a surface hash -> palette hash. The palette hash is either a
-- bitmap with an embedded palette (type 2) or a palette resource (type 3). The
-- engine reads the palette from whichever it is.
--
-- Coverage is partial by nature: 565 of the 1081 no-palette surfaces are mapped.
-- The rest are unreferenced/unused assets or shared sprites reused across scenes
-- with different backgrounds; the engine renders those in neutral grayscale.
--
-- Entries are flat (surface, palette) hash pairs for compactness.
-- ============================================================================

